    <string name="about">About</string>
    <string name="about_text">Nooklings %1$s. Everything stays on the phone: sounds and photos never leave it. The internet is only for the weather. Fonts: m6x11 by Daniel Linssen, Marck Script by Denis Masharov.</string>
    <string name="source">Source code</string>
    <string name="ob_1">Hi. We\'re the nooklings. We live in your room and eat cosiness.</string>
    <string name="ob_1b">Each of us eats our own kind: the cat warmth and tea, the dormouse quiet, the moth something new, the bullfinch voices, the hedgehog weather and walks, the raccoon things made by hand. For now only the cat and the dormouse live here. The rest will come when they smell their kind.</string>
    <string name="ob_2">You don\'t have to do anything special. Just notice when it\'s good.</string>
    <string name="ob_2b">Rain on the umbrella, the kettle, a lamp in the evening, a quiet minute: catch it with the phone. The moment is rolled into a jar and goes on the shelf, and we eat its smell. The jars stay: on a hard day, open one and listen.</string>
    <string name="ob_3">And the window. Which town is outside?</string>
    <string name="ob_3b">Then the window shows that town\'s real sunrise, sunset and weather. You can skip it: the sun will follow your time zone.</string>
    <string name="ob_start">Into the room</string>
